      "math_academy_id": "q-129531",
      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=3.5$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=8.6.$ Find $\\text{Var}[-10X-5Y].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent variables, and $a$ and $b$ are constants, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+bY]={a}^{2}\\text{Var}[X]+{b}^{2}\\text{Var}[Y].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[-10X-5Y]={(-10)}^{2}\\cdot 3.5+{(-5)}^{2}\\cdot 8.6=565.\n$$",
